::  name       mantra weave fields equality gate
::  shape      count - int (@u32) -> lawful - int (@u32)
::  invariant  answers 1 exactly when count is weave fields=3; answers 0 otherwise
::  example    3 -> 1 - 2 -> 0 - 4 -> 0
::  readers    Mantra - Glow Tend a1 unfinished - Ashvini
::  nib        equinox-e257-equality-sixth-v0 - STOA337
::
::  Ashvini equality - sixth pedestal gth cannot speak. The sur shape names
::  a Weave's three fields (lines - next_pos - next_run); this gate decides
::  *exactly*, not by a ceiling.
::
::  Moved two to three on 20260907.182409. Weave grew `next_run` on
::  20260907.173200 and this gate answered 0 for its own subject's count for a
::  lap, green throughout -- not because the binding was missing, yet because
::  the field reader stopped at the doc comment above the new field and
::  reported two. A binding is only as sharp as the reading under it.
|=  sample=@u32
?:  (eq sample 3)  1  0
